    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "When hosting the Olympics or FIFA World Cup host countries tend to economically lose or break even, but that should not discourage economically stable countries from pursuing the chance to host one of these mega sports events. Many other non economic benefits come from hosting such an event which makes the economic risk worth it. This Paper seeks to explain the economics of these events and then show the non economic benefits that make hosting worth it.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
